AB  - A bargaining solution satisfies no individual priorities (NIP) if the following holds: if x is the selected utility allocation and $$\pi x$$ π x is also feasible, where $$\pi $$ π is some permutation, then $$x=\pi x$$ x = π x . I characterize the Nash bargaining solution on the basis of this axiom, non-triviality (the disagreement point is never selected), and scale covariance. An additional characterization is presented for the 2-person case, in which NIP is weakened and symmetry is added.
